      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "I LOVERAIN (2) bounced straight to the front from the rails draw and led until straightening before finishing fifth over 1300m at Darwin last time out. Strong record with Deborah Barton in the irons, including a win. This easier and should be in the finish. MIAMI BABY (5) was out of the money two runs back then again missed the frame last start over 1200m at Darwin, but only beaten 2 lengths into sixth. Looks hard to hold out again. ARIARNE (8) missed the placings two starts back then ran a better race and finished 2.75 lengths away in fifth last time out over 1300m at Darwin. Placed only try course and distance and looks a leading player. BRAVE HERITAGE (9) was below his best last time, finishing sixth and beaten 9 lengths over 1300m at Darwin. Likely improver with top-three prospects. BRYCE (4) gave a sight from a wide gate and faded late. Much better draw this time.",
